=== Findings from the first review

F1  Fixed. eval_at rejects NaN, inf and -inf bindings with Domain, and
    check_finite maps NaN to Domain (src/evaluator.rs lines 71-79, 192-200).
    Pristine probes: 7 of 7 non-finite probes return Err(domain). Break N3
    (guard removed) passes the fixture gate, as expected because JSON cannot
    hold NaN, and the probes catch it: `x` with NaN gives Ok NaN, `x` with inf
    gives Ok Infinity. The unit test non_finite_bindings_are_domain_errors
    feeds the same values; CI run 38733104010 ran it
    (docs/logs/b3-ci-38733104010.log line 190: `... ok`). The choice of
    Domain is recorded in decisions.md (2026-10-15).
F2  Fixed. agree() is relative for nonzero values and exact for zero
    (generate.py lines 338-342); close() in tests/evaluator.rs has no
    absolute rule left (lines 320-326). Break 11 now fails the gate with 29
    failures, including sin(pi) and tan(pi). Break G1 puts the old
    max(1.0, ...) form back in a copy of the generator: the regenerated file
    lets in `(tan(pi) - y) + y` again and the pristine evaluator fails it
    (1 failure). So the filter is load-bearing.
F3  Fixed by reading: TOLERANCE_RELATIVE = 1e-10 and
    ZERO_TOLERANCE_ABSOLUTE = 0.0 are constants in tests/evaluator.rs (lines
    258-259), the header is asserted equal to them (lines 271-288), and
    close() uses only the constants. Not run here: cargo test cannot link.
F6  Fixed. error_cases() runs oracle_classify_error on every label and
    raises on a mismatch (generate.py lines 647-652). Break G2 (exp(800)
    labelled domain) stops the generator: `RuntimeError: error case
    'exp(800)' {}: oracle classified as 'overflow', claimed 'domain'`.
F4  Fixed: progress.md and the end-of-task block say 2,280 (2,130 + 150).
F5  Mostly fixed: generate.py lines 4-5 and 47 and the evaluator's module doc
    say "35 digits, stored as the nearest f64", and decisions.md records that
    reading. Two places still say otherwise: tests/evaluator.rs line 5
    ("computed by mpmath at 30+ digits") and the header
    `"precision_digits": 30`. Not blocking. Fix in the next mathd commit.
F7  Fixed: docs/logs/b3-ci-38733104010.log, a progress.md entry, and the
    end-of-task block on the board.
F8  Fixed: domain_errors_are_errors_not_nan binds x = 0 and asserts
    Domain { arg: -20.0 } (src/evaluator.rs lines 285-289).
F9  Fixed: the comment at tests/evaluator.rs lines 13-16 is rewritten.
F10 Fixed: the progress.md citation is gone (generate.py line 15).

=== New findings

N-a The new gate is exact. N1 (every result 3e-10 relative high) fails 2,098
    of 2,130 value cases; its control at 3e-11 passes with 0 failures. The
    other 32 are the 32 cases whose expected value is exactly 0 (counted in
    the regenerated file), and 0 times anything is 0. Not a defect; it shows
    the gate is 1e-10 and not looser.
N-b Break N2 (0 / 0 passes the division guard) is caught by three
    division_by_zero labels. Before the F1 fix, NaN mapped to Overflow, so
    this break would also have been caught, but by a different kind.
N-c Correction, not blocking: antigravity's B3 end-of-task block cites
    run_strict.mjs, probe.mjs, b3_oracle_check.py, break11_test.py and
    b3harness.wasm. None is in the tree (freebuff noted this at 11:05). The
    first three are mine; their source is now committed as appendices A and B
    of this file. break11_test.py and b3harness.wasm are antigravity's. Say
    in Messages where they are, or that they were scratch files (AGENTS.md
    rule 4).

=== What holds

- 2,130 value cases and 150 error cases, 0 failures under my strict gate.
- 7 of 7 non-finite probes return Err(domain); 4 of 4 literals beyond the f64
  range are parse errors.
- The fixtures regenerate byte for byte (supplement above). Generator stats:
  61 redraws, 12 hostile discards, 31 text-vs-tree mismatches. The first
  review saw 137 mismatches; I did not look at why the number fell.
- Every break I tried was caught: break 11 (29), N1 (2,098), N2 (3), N3
  (2 probes), G1 (1), G2 (generator stops). The N1 control passed, as it
  should.

=== What I could not do

- Run `cargo test`, so F3's header assertion and the unit tests were not run
  under any break here. CI ran them at a605855 (47 unit tests passed).
- Check CI for HEAD: mathd/ has not changed since a605855, so run 38733104010
  is the last mathd run that covers this code.

=== What I am unsure of

- The harness uses Rust's libm port under wasm32, not the glibc libm that CI
  uses. The clean run here and CI both report 0 failures.
- Why the text-vs-tree mismatches fell from 137 to 31. A change in the
  generator's tree shapes would explain it; I did not trace it.

=== Appendix E: rereview.py

"""claude's B3 re-review: one transcript for every check.

Runs from this scratch folder only. mathd/ here is `git archive HEAD mathd`.
The gate is run_strict.mjs (1e-10 relative, exact 0 for expected 0), written
by the reviewer from the work order, never read from eval.json.
Usage: py -3 rereview.py > rereview.out 2>&1
"""
import hashlib, pathlib, shutil, subprocess, sys

HERE = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
H = HERE / "harness"
SRC = HERE / "mathd" / "src" / "evaluator.rs"
FIX = HERE / "mathd" / "fixtures"
WASM = "target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/debug/b3harness.wasm"
PRISTINE = SRC.read_text(encoding="utf-8")


def run(cmd, cwd=H):
    print("$ " + " ".join(str(c) for c in cmd), flush=True)
    d = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True)
    out = (d.stdout + d.stderr).rstrip()
    if out:
        print(out)
    print("[exit %d]" % d.returncode, flush=True)
    return d.returncode


def build():
    return run(["cargo", "build", "--target", "wasm32-unknown-unknown", "-q"])


def gate(json_path):
    return run(["node", "run_strict.mjs", str(json_path), WASM])


def probes_leak():
    """1 when any probe returns a NaN or infinite value, else 0."""
    print("$ node probe.mjs", flush=True)
    out = subprocess.run(["node", "probe.mjs"], cwd=H, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
    print(out.rstrip())
    leaks = [l for l in out.splitlines() if "-> Ok NaN" in l or "-> Ok Infinity" in l or "-> Ok -Infinity" in l]
    print("probes returning a non-finite value: %d" % len(leaks))
    return 1 if leaks else 0


def sha(p):
    return hashlib.sha256(pathlib.Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def section(title):
    print("\n---- " + title, flush=True)


def evaluator_break(name, old, new, check):
    section("break %s" % name)
    assert PRISTINE.count(old) == 1, "anchor not found once: %r" % old
    try:
        SRC.write_text(PRISTINE.replace(old, new), encoding="utf-8")
        print("applied: %r -> %r" % (old, new))
        if build():
            print("BUILD FAILED")
            return
        code = check()
        print("break %s: %s" % (name, "CAUGHT" if code else "NOT CAUGHT"))
    finally:
        SRC.write_text(PRISTINE, encoding="utf-8")
        print("restored:", SRC.read_text(encoding="utf-8") == PRISTINE)


def generator_break(name, old, new, expect):
    section("generator break %s" % name)
    d = HERE / ("gen-" + name)
    shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)
    d.mkdir()
    text = (FIX / "generate.py").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    assert text.count(old) == 1, "anchor not found once: %r" % old
    (d / "generate.py").write_text(text.replace(old, new), encoding="utf-8")
    print("applied to a copy: %r -> %r" % (old, new))
    code = run(["py", "-3", "generate.py"], cwd=d)
    if expect == "generator stops":
        print("generator break %s: %s" % (name, "CAUGHT" if code else "NOT CAUGHT"))
        return
    if code:
        print("generator failed; nothing to gate")
        return
    print("sha256 regenerated %s" % sha(d / "eval.json"))
    print("sha256 committed   %s" % sha(FIX / "eval.json"))
    code = gate(d / "eval.json")
    print("generator break %s: %s" % (name, "CAUGHT" if code else "NOT CAUGHT"))


section("versions")
run(["py", "-3", "-c", "import sys, sympy, mpmath; print('python', sys.version.split()[0], 'sympy', sympy.__version__, 'mpmath', mpmath.__version__)"])
run(["node", "--version"])
run(["rustc", "--version"])

section("pristine: committed fixtures through the strict gate")
build()
gate(FIX / "eval.json")

section("pristine: probes outside the corpus")
probes_leak()

section("fixtures regenerate byte for byte from the committed generator")
g = HERE / "gen-pristine"
shutil.rmtree(g, ignore_errors=True)
g.mkdir()
shutil.copy(FIX / "generate.py", g / "generate.py")
run(["py", "-3", "generate.py"], cwd=g)
print("sha256 regenerated %s" % sha(g / "eval.json"))
print("sha256 committed   %s" % sha(FIX / "eval.json"))
print("identical:", sha(g / "eval.json") == sha(FIX / "eval.json"))

# The first review's break 11: negate every final result below 1e-10.
evaluator_break(
    "11 (negate results below 1e-10)",
    "    eval_inner(expr, bindings)\n}",
    "    let v = eval_inner(expr, bindings)?;\n    Ok(if v.abs() < 1e-10 { -v } else { v })\n}",
    lambda: gate(FIX / "eval.json"),
)
# New: every result 3e-10 relative high. The gate is 1e-10, so this must fail.
evaluator_break(
    "N1 (every result times 1 + 3e-10)",
    "    eval_inner(expr, bindings)\n}",
    "    Ok(eval_inner(expr, bindings)? * (1.0 + 3e-10))\n}",
    lambda: gate(FIX / "eval.json"),
)
# Control for N1: 3e-11 is inside the gate, so this one should pass.
evaluator_break(
    "N1-control (every result times 1 + 3e-11; should NOT be caught)",
    "    eval_inner(expr, bindings)\n}",
    "    Ok(eval_inner(expr, bindings)? * (1.0 + 3e-11))\n}",
    lambda: gate(FIX / "eval.json"),
)
# New: 0/0 slips past the division guard. NaN now maps to Domain, so the
# fixture's division_by_zero labels must catch the wrong kind.
evaluator_break(
    "N2 (0 / 0 passes the division guard)",
    "            if r == 0.0 {\n                return Err(EvalError::DivisionByZero { numerator: l });",
    "            if r == 0.0 && l != 0.0 {\n                return Err(EvalError::DivisionByZero { numerator: l });",
    lambda: gate(FIX / "eval.json"),
)
# New: the F1 guard on bindings removed. JSON cannot carry NaN, so the
# fixture gate cannot see this; the probes and the unit test
# non_finite_bindings_are_domain_errors (not runnable here) must.
evaluator_break(
    "N3 (non-finite binding guard removed; judged by probes)",
    "            if !val.is_finite() {\n                return Err(EvalError::Domain { arg: val });\n            }\n            Ok(val)",
    "            Ok(val)",
    lambda: (gate(FIX / "eval.json"), probes_leak())[1],
)
# F2's filter: put back the old absolute-below-1 agreement and regenerate.
generator_break(
    "G1 (agree() absolute below 1 again)",
    "    return abs(a - b) <= F64_CONSISTENCY * abs(b)",
    "    return abs(a - b) <= F64_CONSISTENCY * max(1.0, abs(a), abs(b))",
    "gate fails",
)
# F6: a wrong hand label must stop the generator.
generator_break(
    "G2 (exp(800) labelled domain)",
    '("exp(800)", {}, "overflow"),',
    '("exp(800)", {}, "domain"),',
    "generator stops",
)

section("end")
build()
print("pristine rebuilt; source identical to HEAD copy:", SRC.read_text(encoding="utf-8") == PRISTINE)

VERDICT: PASS (F1, F2, F3, F6 fixed; F5 wording and N-c citations to correct in Messages or the next mathd commit)
